-- ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Worldforged pickups: the placements the realm map records, and nothing else
-- ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- The realm map is the authority for where a worldforged pickup stands. It plots every one of
-- them, by name, in the zone it was found in, and this migration makes the world stand exactly
-- that: the pickups the realm has, each once, each at the place the map marks it.
--
-- WHAT IT REPLACES
-- The earlier passes placed a pickup wherever any single record put it - one per recorded
-- position, per realm, per zone dump, per loot pin. That is why an object can be found several
-- times over in one zone and why some stand where the realm never had them. Those rows are
-- cleared here (every spawn of a `worldforged_pickup` template in the module's own guid blocks)
-- and this file's set is the whole of what remains.
--
-- WHERE EACH VALUE COMES FROM
--   which pickup   the map's name. The realm names a pickup after the item it holds, so that
--                  name is usually both; where the name is a prop ('Old Grave', 'Waterlogged
--                  Chest', 'Black Powder Barrel') the realm has an object of precisely that
--                  name and its loot row names the item, so the object is the one the map means.
--   position       the map's own marker, converted to world coordinates through each zone's own
--                  world rectangle. Against the archive's loot pins - recorded world positions
--                  for the same item in the same zone - the conversion agrees to a median of
--                  2.5 yd over 1,872 markers.
--   height         never invented. In order of use: the height the pickup itself already
--                  stands at in this world; the height the client recorded for that object at
--                  that spot; the floor the realm's own occupants (props, doors, chairs,
--                  creatures) stand on within 70 yd, which matters because a marker's own
--                  coordinate carries a few yards of slack and a few yards sideways on a
--                  slope is tens of yards of height; the floor the pickups around it share;
--                  and only where the realm has put nothing at all, the server's own terrain,
--                  read exactly as the core reads it.
--   template       for a pickup the realm already has, its own entry and appearance are used
--                  untouched. A name the realm has no pickup for is not placed, rather than
--                  invented.
--
-- A marker that pairs with a mystic scroll at the same spot is a scroll source and is left out:
-- scrolls are not part of this restoration.
--
-- Totals: 2480 placements over 76 zones, 1574 pickup objects.
-- 45 markers are left unplaced because nothing in the realm states their height; they are
-- named at the end of this file rather than stood on a guess.
-- ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

DELETE `g` FROM `gameobject` `g`
  JOIN `gameobject_template` `t` ON `t`.`entry` = `g`.`id`
 WHERE `t`.`ScriptName` = 'worldforged_pickup'
   AND (`g`.`guid` BETWEEN 6900001 AND 6939999 OR `g`.`guid` BETWEEN 6940001 AND 6999999);

INSERT INTO `gameobject` (`guid`, `id`, `map`, `zoneId`, `areaId`, `spawnMask`, `phaseMask`,
                          `position_x`, `position_y`, `position_z`, `orientation`, `rotation0`,
                          `rotation1`, `rotation2`, `rotation3`, `spawntimesecs`, `animprogress`,
